<Shell title="Aero · Public evidence" description="What Aero has demonstrated, what failed, and what remains untested. Inspect retained technical papers, solver evidence and external benchmark chronology." path="/software/aero/evidence/">
<header><p class="eyebrow">AERO / CANONICAL PUBLIC EVIDENCE INDEX</p><h1>What has Aero actually demonstrated?</h1><p>Bounded verification and rejection behavior. Analytical agreement is not experimental validation; a <strong>FAIL can be the correct engineering outcome.</strong></p></header>
<nav class="links" aria-label="Evidence sections"><a href="#retained">Retained studies</a><a href="#external-benchmarks">External Benchmarks</a><a href="#artifacts">Papers / raw artifacts</a><a href="#limits">Meaning of the claims</a></nav>
<section id="retained"><h2>Inspect the outcomes—not just the green checks.</h2><div class="filters" aria-label="Filter by discipline">{['All','CFD','Thermal','Structural','CAD / Geometry'].map((x,i)=><button data-filter={x} aria-pressed={i===0}>{x}</button>)}</div><p data-filter-count class="subtle" role="status">7 evidence items</p><div class="cards">
<article data-disciplines="CFD Thermal"><p class="eyebrow">CFD · FAILURE INVESTIGATION</p><span class="status failed">NUMERICAL FAIL · INVESTIGATION COMPLETE</span><h3>HARCC S4 Part II: solver-control diagnosis</h3><p class="metric">v8 moved h/e down and U up; all target gates still fail.</p><p>Includes a valid pressure-cap test, an invalid configuration test kept visible, and a corrected one-versus-two outer-corrector comparison. The stop rule ended the solver-control branch without a v9.</p><p class="subtle">No mesh independence, matched experimental validation, wall-treatment suitability, or design readiness is claimed.</p><div class="links"><a href="/software/aero/evidence/benchmarks/harcc-s4-part2/">Read Part II and inspect retained logs →</a><a href="/software/aero/evidence/benchmarks/">Benchmark register</a></div></article>
<article data-disciplines="CFD"><p class="eyebrow">CFD · VERIFICATION + NEGATIVE CONTROLS</p><span class="status mixed">MIXED</span><h3>Verification Bench Rev 1.0</h3><p class="metric">{v.pipe[2].reference_error_pct.toFixed(3)}% fine-grid error. Two real failures.</p><p>Three pipe grids agree with Poiseuille within 2%. Their errors decrease from {v.pipe[0].reference_error_pct.toFixed(3)}% to {v.pipe[1].reference_error_pct.toFixed(3)}% to {v.pipe[2].reference_error_pct.toFixed(3)}%. The negative controls miss by {v.pipe[3].reference_error_pct.toFixed(3)}% and {v.pipe[4].reference_error_pct.toFixed(3)}%.</p><p>Both nozzle treatments fail near-wall readiness. y+ and all-component residual histories distinguish an active-field convergence problem from an ill-conditioned negligible component.</p><p class="subtle">7 new OpenFOAM runs · {v.archive_file_count} hashed archive files, including CAD and 5 retained CalculiX decks · 7-page paper. Criteria correction disclosed; not a blinded preregistration.</p><div class="links"><a href="/software/aero/verification/">Inspect the frozen bench →</a><a href="/demos/aero/verification-bench-v1/paper.pdf">Paper ↗</a></div><details><summary>Scope, reference and retained artifacts</summary><p>Analytical pipe verification and numerical-readiness rejection, not an experiment or a general nozzle validation. The original Rev 1.0 page, results, and bundle remain frozen.</p><div class="links"><a href="/demos/aero/verification-bench-v1/reproducibility.zip">Full decks ↓</a><a href="/demos/aero/verification-bench-v1/summary.json">Results JSON</a><a href="/demos/aero/verification-bench-v1/manifest.json">SHA-256 manifest</a></div></details></article>
<article data-disciplines="CFD"><p class="eyebrow">CFD · ANALYTICAL BENCHMARK</p><span class="status bounded">BOUNDED PASS</span><h3>Channel pressure-budget study</h3><p class="metric">{d.channel.selected_gap_mm} mm is the smallest tested passing gap.</p><p>{d.channel.solves} OpenFOAM solves: 3 gaps × 3 grids. At 25 mL/s and a 40 Pa budget, the fine-grid losses are {d.channel.variants.map(x=>x.pressure_drop_pa.toFixed(3)).join(', ')} Pa for 1.5, 2.0 and 2.5 mm gaps.</p><p>The smaller gaps fail the budget even though numerical checks pass. The 2.5 mm recommendation includes the declared numerical allowance.</p><p class="subtle">{d.channel.paper_artifacts} hashed paper-package artifacts · analytical parallel-plate comparison, profile, residual and conservation checks. Not a sidewall, fitting-loss, or hardware validation.</p><div class="links"><a href="/demos/aero/channel-study-v1/research-paper.pdf">Paper ↗</a><a href="/software/aero/current/?study=channel">Explore inputs →</a></div><details><summary>Conditions, distinct examples and artifacts</summary><p>This capability study uses 25 mL/s / 40 Pa. The separate interactive default uses 20 mL/s / 70 Pa; their recommendations are not interchangeable.</p><div class="links"><a href="/demos/aero/channel-study-v1/research-paper-sources.zip">Reproduction sources ↓</a><a href="/demos/aero/channel-study-v1/changed-inputs-result.json">Studied result JSON</a><a href="/demos/aero/channel-study-v1/research-paper-manifest.json">Paper hashes</a></div></details></article>
<article data-disciplines="Thermal"><p class="eyebrow">THERMAL · ANALYTICAL SCREENING</p><span class="status bounded">BOUNDED PASS</span><h3>Cooling-channel layout decision</h3><p class="metric">Layout {d.thermal.selected_layout}: two 2 mm passages.</p><p>Three layouts assessed under a 100 W load, 72 °C inner-wall limit and 2 kPa straight-channel pressure budget. Nominal and adverse scenarios are retained.</p><p>Energy closure error: {d.thermal.energy_relative_error}. The final radial heat-transfer check differs from its analytical reference by {d.thermal.radial_final_error_pct.toFixed(6)}%.</p><p class="subtle">{d.thermal.paper_artifacts} hashed paper-package artifacts. Analytical thermal screening—not thermal CFD or experimental validation. Manifold, contact and boiling effects remain outside the model.</p><div class="links"><a href="/demos/aero/cooling-study-v1/research-paper.pdf">Paper ↗</a><a href="/software/aero/cooling/">Explore the study →</a></div><details><summary>Calculation sources and artifacts</summary><div class="links"><a href="/demos/aero/cooling-study-v1/research-paper-sources.zip">LaTeX + evidence ↓</a><a href="/demos/aero/cooling-study-v1/result.json">Results JSON</a><a href="/demos/aero/cooling-study-v1/research-paper-manifest.json">Paper hashes</a></div></details></article>
<article data-disciplines="Thermal Structural"><p class="eyebrow">THERMAL + STRUCTURAL · SYNTHETIC PREBENCHMARK</p><span class="status mixed">PREBENCHMARK</span><h3>Samarmad-derived PCHE gate pack</h3><p class="metric">10 runnable gates passed; paper-specific gates remain separate.</p><p>A source-derived printed-circuit heat-exchanger packet exercises prediction freezing, criteria hashing, curved-interface pressure and heat-rate transfer, generic OpenFOAM CHT, and generic three-level CalculiX acceptance.</p><p class="subtle">These six operating points are synthetic pipeline tests—not publication results. The later Samarmad-specific run has its own failed numerical outcome and unscored experimental comparison.</p><div class="links"><a href="/software/aero/evidence/benchmarks/samarmad-synthetic/">Inspect the synthetic prebenchmark →</a><a href="/demos/aero/samarmad-synthetic-prebenchmark-v1/README.md">Public record ↗</a><a href="/software/aero/evidence/benchmarks/samarmad-pche-publication-v1/">Read the publication-targeted run →</a></div></article>
<article data-disciplines="Structural Thermal"><p class="eyebrow">STRUCTURAL · NUMERICAL ADEQUACY + REJECTION</p><span class="status mixed">MIXED</span><h3>CalculiX structural extension</h3><p class="metric">{d.structural.solves} retained solves. Seven configurations.</p><p>Bracket, pressure tubes, a port and thermal restraint were tested at three mesh levels. The port fails mesh sensitivity. The thermal-gradient case passes numerical checks but fails its stress requirement.</p><p>Pressure-tube numerical acceptability remains NOT ESTABLISHED with reaction-balance evidence missing. Every configuration retains design readiness NOT ESTABLISHED.</p><p class="subtle">CalculiX 2.20 · Gmsh / CadQuery. Decks and analytical comparisons are bounded evidence, not validated structural design capability.</p><div class="links"><a href="/demos/aero/fea-v1/README.html">Acceptance report →</a><a href="/software/aero/current/?case=fea-bracket-20260912">Explore a saved case →</a></div><details><summary>Per-configuration gates and manifests</summary><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Configuration</th><th>Numerical</th><th>Requirements</th></tr></thead><tbody>{d.structural.cases.map(r=><tr><td><a href={r.url}>{r.case}</a><br/><a href={r.manifest}>Manifest</a></td><td>{r.numerical}</td><td>{r.requirements}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div><p>All 7 public configuration manifests were checked against their retained files: {d.structural.manifest_mismatches.length} mismatches. The Verification Bench bundle contains 5 of these retained solve decks, not all 21.</p><a href="/demos/aero/verification-bench-v1/reproducibility.zip">Download retained deck subset ↓</a></details></article>
<article data-disciplines="CAD / Geometry"><p class="eyebrow">CAD / GEOMETRY · NEGATIVE CONTROL</p><span class="status failed">FAIL — correctly rejected</span><h3>Imported manifold with a detached sliver</h3><p class="metric">2 solids. Solver not submitted.</p><p>The STEP fixture has intersecting ports and fillets. The intact reimport passes topology only; the defective variant violates the single-solid intake contract. No silent deletion or automatic repair.</p><p class="subtle">Two synthetic STEP reimports · OpenCASCADE / CadQuery. This does not establish general imported-CAD robustness.</p><div class="links"><a href="/software/aero/verification/#cad">Inspect geometry and rejection →</a><a href="/demos/aero/verification-bench-v1/reproducibility.zip">Original STEP + evidence ↓</a></div></article>
</div></section>
<section id="external-benchmarks"><p class="eyebrow">EXTERNAL BENCHMARKS</p><h2>Independent measurements. A frozen prediction.</h2><article><span class:list={['status',challenge.result==='FAIL'?'failed':'pending']}>{challenge.has_comparison ? challenge.result : 'RUNNING · NOT EVALUATED'}</span><h3>Aero Blind Validation Challenge 01</h3><p>NASA TM-4074 Table XIII: 18 operating points, three grids per point, and 36 experimental targets. Criteria and execution code were publicly committed before production. {challenge.completed} / {challenge.total} attempts finished in the published snapshot.</p><p class="subtle">Reference withheld from solver execution; supervisory setup was not fully blinded. Numerical failures remain visible.</p><div class="links"><a class="primary" href="/software/aero/evidence/benchmarks/blind-validation-01/">Inspect results and chronology →</a><a href="/software/aero/evidence/benchmarks/">All external benchmarks →</a></div></article></section>
<section id="artifacts"><h2>Technical papers / artifacts</h2><p>The links above lead to the original versioned records. This index does not replace or revise them.</p><div class="links"><a href="/demos/aero/evidence-index-v1/index.json">Audited index + source hashes</a><a href="/software/aero/verification/#reproduce">Permanent reproduction bundle</a><a href="/software/aero/evidence/benchmarks/blind-validation-01/#downloads">Challenge protocol + source package</a></div><p class="subtle">62 committed source artifacts audited. Source snapshot <code>{d.source_commit}</code>. Index hashes establish identity; they do not independently establish scientific validity.</p></section>
<section id="limits" class="boundary"><h2>Different evidence answers different questions.</h2><ul><li><strong>Verification / analytical benchmarking:</strong> agreement with a known mathematical solution for stated assumptions.</li><li><strong>Numerical adequacy:</strong> mesh, residual, conservation and wall-treatment checks. Necessary, not sufficient for physical accuracy.</li><li><strong>Negative controls / rejection:</strong> deliberately deficient conditions must not be promoted as accepted predictions.</li><li><strong>External validation:</strong> comparison with independent experimental measurements, subject to the declared numerical and modeling limitations.</li><li><strong>Reproducibility:</strong> retained inputs, versions, outputs and hashes permit inspection and reruns—not a guarantee of solver accuracy.</li><li><strong>Model behavior:</strong> context, routing, explanation, investigation, and claim-verification behavior; this is not physical-validation evidence.</li><li><strong>Infrastructure / efficiency qualification:</strong> payload reduction, scoped tools, portability, and deterministic guardrails; an infrastructure pass is not an engineering-capability pass.</li></ul><p>Failures remain evidence: HARCC and Samarmad numerical failures, CalculiX NOT_ESTABLISHED states, port mesh-sensitivity and thermal-gradient requirement failures, imported-CAD rejection, the Blind Validation Challenge failure, and CEP-01 model qualification still open. No item establishes universal Aero validation, certification, autonomous design authority or design readiness.</p></section>
<script>const buttons=document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-filter]');const cards=document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-disciplines]');for(const b of buttons)b.addEventListener('click',()=>{for(const other of buttons)other.setAttribute('aria-pressed',String(other===b));let n=0;for(const card of cards){card.hidden=b.dataset.filter!=='All'&&!card.dataset.disciplines?.includes(b.dataset.filter!);if(!card.hidden)n++;}document.querySelector('[data-filter-count]')!.textContent=`${n} evidence item${n===1?'':'s'}`;});</script>
</Shell>
